  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vampire Touched joins the Fey Touched and Shadow Touched feats, offering access to some low level spells without class spell lists restrictions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Any mental stat. Perfect for spellcasters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-vampire-magic",
      "heading": "Vampire Magic",
      "sourceAnchor": "vampire-magic",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampire-magic-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Spider Climb is a decent spell, especially if you don’t have access to flight, but you’re here for the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Enchantment/Illusion",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells?filter-search=&filter-level=1&filter-school=6&filter-school=8&filter-verbal=&filter-somatic=&filter-material=&filter-concentration=&filter-ritual=&filter-partnered-content=f"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " spell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampire-magic-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Animal Friendship"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": If you want to deal with\n    animals, get Ritual Caster and cast Speak with Animals.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bane"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Not useful often enough to justify.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Bless"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A fantastic buff, but as you gain\n    levels you’re unlikely to commit Concentration to it.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Charm Person"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful, and\n    it’s already on a ton of spell lists.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Color Spray"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Awful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Command"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Powerful, versatile, and\n    upcasting to add more targets is great.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Compelled Duel"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Most characters don’t have\n    access to any sort of taunt mechanic. Gish builds, especially durable ones\n    like Eldritch Knights, may get a lot of value out of this.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Disguise Self"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationally useful.\n    Very few games can justify investing a feat to get this spell.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Dissonant Whispers"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Break grapples and\n    force the target to trigger Opportunity Attacks. The damage is weak, and\n    there’s no reason to upcast it, but it’s still decent.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Distort Value"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Heroism"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": A decent buff, but as you gain\n    levels you’re unlikely to commit Concentration to it.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Hex"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Potentially great for martial\n    characters that make numerous attacks. Also remember that it imposes\n    Disadvantage on Ability Checks for one Ability of your choice, so you can\n    use this to debuff Wisdom so that your target is bad at Perception.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Illusory Script"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Silent Image",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/spells/practical-guide-to-illusions/&sa=D&source=editors&ust=1764274659051230&usg=AOvVaw1Y8abhl-wx9EB8cg6uEHQb"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Very useful, but you can also take the Eldritch Adept feat to get Misty\n    Visions, which lets you cast Silent Image at will without a spell slot.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Silvery Barbs",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd-5es-silvery-barbs/&sa=D&source=editors&ust=1764274659052267&usg=AOvVaw1z5s5HasL4rqI1ziIkJzNy"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Insanely powerful.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sleep"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": An incredible save-or-suck spell at\n    any level.\n  "
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n    "
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Tasha’s Hideous Laughter"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Sleep is an\n    easier save-or-suck because your target(s) only get one additional save\n    instead of one every round. But this is also better at targeting multiple\n    creatures, which may be worthwhile.\n  "
              }
            ]
          ],
